WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.280
Welcome back, champ!

2
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:17.530
Last time: game rules · Unit 3 done!

3
00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:23.790
Unit 4 · Being Smart and Safe With AI

4
00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:28.950
Chapter 1 · Is AI Fair?

5
00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:40.860
Can a computer be fair, or unfair?

6
00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:51.210
Meet Ishaan and his hat finder

7
00:00:51.210 --> 00:01:05.160
He teaches it with 50 photos… all red caps

8
00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:11.470
Red cap? "Hat!" Perfect.

9
00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:21.330
Nani's blue woolly cap? "Not a hat!"

10
00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:29.660
Why did it get it wrong? Think!

11
00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:37.960
Training examples: what AI learns from

12
00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:49.320
The pattern it found: "hats are red"

13
00:01:49.320 --> 00:02:01.410
Only seen red apples? A green one looks odd!

14
00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:14.540
Not mean. It just didn't learn enough.

15
00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:26.850
FAIR = works well for everyone

16
00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:38.990
Unfair AI (bias): not enough kinds of examples

17
00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:45.220
One kind of example → confused by others

18
00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:55.980
Add blue, green, striped, woolly hats!

19
00:02:55.980 --> 00:03:07.190
VARIETY = many different kinds

20
00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:13.000
Nani's cap? "Hat!" Fixed!

21
00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:22.580
Only a red crayon? No green tree, no blue sky!

22
00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:26.820
Many colours → a better picture

23
00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:39.460
Many kinds of examples → a fairer AI

24
00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:53.280
Voice helper learned only grown-up voices

25
00:03:53.280 --> 00:04:03.090
Face unlock needs many kinds of faces

26
00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:08.930
A doctor's AI needs X-rays from everyone

27
00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:16.570
People must test it works for everyone

28
00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:38.880
Which photos are fairer for a dog finder?

29
00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:49.630
Set B! 100 of one kind still isn't variety

30
00:04:49.630 --> 00:05:04.710
Finish it: "AI needs ___ examples."

31
00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:12.970
AI needs MANY KINDS OF examples!

32
00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:27.920
True or false: AI is fair automatically?

33
00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:36.900
FALSE! AI is only as fair as its examples

34
00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:40.850
Your turn: practice check

35
00:05:40.850 --> 00:05:52.640
Only saw red hats. What about a blue hat?

36
00:05:52.640 --> 00:06:05.410
May say "not a hat". It needs many kinds!

37
00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:10.030
AI learns only from its examples

38
00:06:10.030 --> 00:06:14.950
One kind of example → unfair AI

39
00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:19.900
AI needs many kinds of examples

40
00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:23.670
More variety → fairer helpers

41
00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:29.900
Chapter 1 done!

42
00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:36.700
Next: Quiz · Tap Finish
